          "informationUri": "https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff",
          "name": "ruff",
          "rules": [
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "## What it does\nChecks for functions with a high `McCabe` complexity.\n\n## Why is this bad?\nThe `McCabe` complexity of a function is a measure of the complexity of\nthe control flow graph of the function. It is calculated by adding\none to the number of decision points in the function. A decision\npoint is a place in the code where the program has a choice of two\nor more paths to follow.\n\nFunctions with a high complexity are hard to understand and maintain.\n\n## Example\n```python\ndef normalize_status(status):\n    if status == \"new\":\n        return \"queued\"\n    if status == \"queued\":\n        return \"running\"\n    if status == \"running\":\n        return \"done\"\n    if status == \"failed\":\n        return \"retry\"\n    if status == \"cancelled\":\n        return \"closed\"\n    return \"unknown\"\n```\n\nUse instead:\n\n```python\nSTATUS_TRANSITIONS = {\n    \"new\": \"queued\",\n    \"queued\": \"running\",\n    \"running\": \"done\",\n    \"failed\": \"retry\",\n    \"cancelled\": \"closed\",\n}\n\n\ndef normalize_status(status):\n    return STATUS_TRANSITIONS.get(status, \"unknown\")\n```\n\nNote that this example assumes a `lint.mccabe.max-complexity` of 5 or less to trigger a\ndiagnostic because the initial code only has a complexity of 6.\n\n## Options\n- `lint.mccabe.max-complexity`\n"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "`{name}` is too complex ({complexity} > {max_complexity})"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.astral.sh/ruff/rules/complex-structure",
              "id": "C901",
              "properties": {
                "id": "C901",
                "kind": "mccabe",
                "name": "complex-structure",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "`{name}` is too complex ({complexity} > {max_complexity})"
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.17.1"
        }
      }
